{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/676742-on-pacts-and-imposters","id":676742,"title":"On Pacts and Imposters.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-24T13:08:49-07:00","id":676742,"title":"On Pacts and Imposters.","content":"Let's say some sort of minor shapeshifted locks a man in his basement and impersonates him - completely successfully - for a year. He runs into a Demon and offers up his relationship to his victim's best friend in the Pact. What happens from the best friend's point of view? <br /> <br /> An odd question, but one that might be coming up in a game of mine soon and I'm curious as to the options. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T13:41:36-07:00","id":676842,"title":"","content":"What kind of shapeshifter? Does it have some kind of true form or other guise? Does the friend know the shapeshifter by another guise as well, or only as the impersonated victim?<br /> <br /> The major trick here, to my mind, is that you can't sell somebody a relationship you don't have. The shapeshifter does not have a relationship with the friend as the impersonated victim. That's the victim's to sell, and the shapeshifter is only taking advantage of it.<br /> <br /> Things start to get complicated when the ruse goes on so long that the friend associates behavior and memories unique to the impostor as strongly with the victim as she does the victim's own actions. Those new associations are the shapeshifter's to sell, and if sold without the demon continuing the impersonation, might possibly split the friend's associations and memories from having one person she knows to having two people she knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T13:47:15-07:00","id":676844,"title":"","content":"Excellent questions/points!<br /> <br /> The Best Friend doesn't know the shapeshifter in any other form -- effectively, the shapeshifter was born when it adopted the guise of the Victim. If it was a temporary thing -- say, someone pretended to be someone and then immediately went to sign a Pact, that'd be one thing. But in this case, the Imposter has had an active and ongoing relationship with the Best Friend for a year. You last paragraph is probably where I'd lean to -- that the Best Friend now perceives two people. Or, since I seem to recall there being a bit of innate mental acrobatics involved for people affected, might the Best Friend turn the perception of two people into &quot;man, my buddy changed a LOT a year ago&quot; as a way to rationalize away the madness inherit in you randomly feeling like your best friend is two separate people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T14:15:44-07:00","id":676855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/676742-on-pacts-and-imposters?p=676844#post676844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, since I seem to recall there being a bit of innate mental acrobatics involved for people affected, might the Best Friend turn the perception of two people into &quot;man, my buddy changed a LOT a year ago&quot; as a way to rationalize away the madness inherit in you randomly feeling like your best friend is two separate people?</div> </div> </div> </div>The real buddy's still out there, though, and he hasn't sold his relationship, so that's intact. If he were to escape and run into his old friend post-pact, she would still remember him and all the things they did together. What I had in mind by splitting into two people is that, post-pact, she remembers having two distinct friends: one friend who corresponds to the real buddy, and another friend who showed up after the real buddy disappeared somehow, corresponding now to the demon with the memories of what she did with the fake buddy.<br /> <br /> Bizarrely, this would then imply that the shapeshifter could then resume impersonating the real buddy, though it would have to start from square one without any foundational work laid in the interim to shore up its little-C cover story, and come up with a reason why she &quot;hasn't seen him around&quot; for a year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T05:05:22-07:00","id":677507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/676742-on-pacts-and-imposters#post676742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say some sort of minor shapeshifted locks a man in his basement and impersonates him - completely successfully - for a year. He runs into a Demon and offers up his relationship to his victim's best friend in the Pact. What happens from the best friend's point of view?<br /> <br /> An odd question, but one that might be coming up in a game of mine soon and I'm curious as to the options. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>The imposter can sell the relationship with Joe Smith. Which is &quot;pretending to be best friend&quot; and all the fall otu that would result from it. Jessica, whom the imposter is posing as, has a relationship of &quot;best friend before kidnapping&quot; with Joe Smith. Relationships aren't static things. Its best to think in terms of individuals, and not &quot;roles&quot; for that way lies the madness of the God Machine. Or just easier to think about in terms the pact.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, here's a little discussed part of Demon. It appears that as you absorb new relationships into your Cover, it changes your appearance slightly. You see it hinted at in the fiction. So, by buying the Imposter-of-friend relationship, you'll shift to look a bit like Jessica. People's memories and all the photographs will shift to match as well. So, Jessica, when she breaks out, people will be able to see how the imposter managed to look like her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-25-2015, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}